    "result_text": "Build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with both findings \u2014 they point at the same structural issue \u2014 and addressed them together.\n\n**What changed:** The content-type/status wrapping now lives in exactly one place. I extended the shared `ProblemDetails` helper with two `response(...)` methods:\n\n```java\nstatic ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> response(Exception ex, HttpStatus status, String detail) {\n    return response(build(ex, status, detail));\n}\nstatic ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> response(ProblemDetail detail) {\n    return ResponseEntity.status(detail.getStatus())\n            .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_PROBLEM_JSON)\n            .body(detail);\n}\n```\n\nEvery escalation handler that emits a `ProblemDetail` now produces it identically:\n\n- The 9 owner handlers (400/409/429) collapse to a single `response.send(ProblemDetails.response(ex, HttpStatus.X, \"...\"))` \u2014 status named once, no repeated `.contentType(...)`, and the now-unused `MediaType` import removed from each.\n- The 3 pre-existing handlers (`DataIntegrityViolation`, `General`, `Forbidden`) were migrated to the same one-liner \u2014 this also resolves Finding 1, since they previously omitted the content type. They now consistently emit `application/problem+json` too.\n- `ValidationExceptionHandler` enriches the body with `schemaValidationErrors` before sending, so it uses the `response(ProblemDetail)` overload (status taken from the body) rather than rebuilding.\n\n**One deliberate choice worth flagging:** the three formerly-migrated handlers (`DataIntegrityViolation` \u2192 404, `General` \u2192 500, `Forbidden` \u2192 403) now set the `application/problem+json` content type where before they let it default to `application/json`. This is the single-convention outcome Finding 1 asked for, it's correct per RFC7807 since they already return `ProblemDetail` bodies, and it falls outside the 400/409/429 scope of the acceptance test, so behaviour the tests pin is unchanged.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, acceptance test green.",
